  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **0-indexed** integer array `nums`. A pair of indices `(i, j)` is a **bad pair** if `i < j` and `j - i != nums[j] - nums[i]`.\n\nOutput *the total number of **bad pairs** in* `nums`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [4,1,3,3]\nOutput: 5\nExplanation: The pair (0, 1) is a bad pair since 1 - 0 != 1 - 4.\nThe pair (0, 2) is a bad pair since 2 - 0 != 3 - 4, 2 != -1.\nThe pair (0, 3) is a bad pair since 3 - 0 != 3 - 4, 3 != -1.\nThe pair (1, 2) is a bad pair since 2 - 1 != 3 - 1, 1 != 2.\nThe pair (2, 3) is a bad pair since 3 - 2 != 3 - 3, 1 != 0.\nThere are a total of 5 bad pairs, so we return 5.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,5]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: There are no bad pairs.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
